  "term": "pad",
  "says": "A string-machine descendant: two saws slightly detuned (or one with unison), a slow swell in and a long release, a low-pass sitting half closed with moderate key follow, an ensemble chorus for width, no velocity sensitivity. What makes it a pad is the envelope (attack above half a second) and the width; what keeps it usable is that the mono sum does not lose its body (within 6 dB of the stereo level).",
